# Cadence Project Guidelines & Architecture Rules

## Core Tech Stack
- Framework: TanStack Start with React 19 (Strictly NOT Next.js).
- Runtime & Package Manager: Bun (Use `bun` commands, avoid `npm` where possible).
- Styling: Tailwind CSS & Lucide React icons.
- Data Storage: Local-first architecture using IndexedDB and LocalStorage.

## Code Standards & Language
- ALL code comments and technical documentation must strictly be written in English.
- Use explicit TypeScript types. Avoid using `any`.
- Strictly use `crypto.randomUUID()` for all newly generated entity IDs (habits, routines, goals, quit items). Never use sequential integers.
- Always include an ISO string `updatedAt` timestamp when modifying or creating data models.

## UI & Layout Integrity
- Do NOT alter, displace, or remove the Bottom Navigation bar or the Top Header layout.
- Preserve all existing touch gesture handlers, long-press behaviors, and drag-and-drop sensors.
- Maintain responsive padding and mobile Safe-Area insets (`pb-safe`).

## PWA & Offline Safety
- Keep the service worker registration SSR-safe (only in client mounts / `useEffect`).
- Never introduce network calls that break offline functionality.
- Ensure all deep-link routes remain navigable offline.